From: Petr Wozniak <petr.wozniak@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] map-controller: phase2 recovery
Signed-off-by: Petr Wozniak <petr.wozniak@gmail.com>

map-controller: Phase 2 DB recovery - db_restore() on controller boot

ADR-0003 Phase 2 (the flagship payoff of the mapdb persistence layer): on
controller boot, hydrate the live model from mapc.db so the mesh topology is
"warm" at t=0 and a powercycle recovers deterministically instead of a cold
rediscovery. The inverse of the Phase-1 write hooks, using the same
engine-neutral mapdb read primitives (mapdb_prepare/step/column_*/finalize).

- src/db/mapc_sync.c: add db_restore() + reverse marshalling helpers
  (str2mac/hex2bytes) and per-table restore functions for the 7 recovery-graph
  tables (agent/radio/operating_class/radio_caps/bss/topology_link). It is a
  strict no-op on a fresh/empty DB (guarded by an agent-count probe) so it never
  perturbs the normal cold-boot discovery + Phase-1 write path. Warm entries are
  seeded via the keyed find-or-alloc constructors (in-place upsert, no dup);
  live Topology/Cap responses confirm-or-overwrite them, and any ghost ages out
  via the existing NODE_EXPIRE_TIME(65s) path. It deliberately does NOT force
  c->topology.valid (that would skip the live topology build that persists
  agent/radio/bss) - the live tree build re-confirms and re-writes.
- src/db/mapc_sync.h: db_restore() prototype.
- src/cntlr.c: include db/mapc_sync.h and call db_restore(c) in run_controller()
  after the AL-MAC + UCI nodelist are ready, before the discovery timers arm.

No struct fields added (append-only ABI rule preserved). Best-effort: a NULL
c->db or any prepare/step error degrades to today's cold-discovery behaviour.
--- a/src/db/mapc_sync.c
+++ b/src/db/mapc_sync.c
@@ -28,6 +28,7 @@
 #include "db/mapdb.h"
 #include "db/mapc_sync.h"
 #include "utils/debug.h"
+#include "timeutils.h"
 
 /* ---- small marshalling helpers ---------------------------------------- */
 
@@ -492,3 +493,326 @@
 	if (mapdb_exec(c->db, "PRAGMA wal_checkpoint(TRUNCATE);") != MAPDB_OK)
 		warn("mapc_sync: wal_checkpoint: %s\n", mapdb_last_error(c->db));
 }
